.TH INDI_SCOPELINK 1 "2026-08-12" "indi-scopelink 1.0" "INDI Drivers"
.SH NAME
indi_scopelink \- INDI driver for the Astrolabs ScopeLink telescope controller
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B indiserver
.RI [ options ]
.B indi_scopelink
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B indi_scopelink
publishes one Astrolabs ScopeLink controller as a single INDI device. It is a driver, not a program to
run by hand: an INDI server starts it and clients such as KStars or Ekos talk to it over the server.
.PP
One USB connection carries a stepper focuser, a motorised front flap over the telescope aperture, a flat
panel, two mirror cooling fans and, depending on the hardware generation, two auxiliary power outputs and
a powered USB hub. The driver claims the INDI focuser, light box and auxiliary interfaces on every
controller, and the dust cap interface as well when the front flap is fitted and calibrated.
.PP
What a controller offers is read out of the hardware when the driver connects, so properties that a given
generation does not have are never published rather than being published and failing.
.SH USAGE
Start the driver under an INDI server:
.PP
.RS
.B indiserver -v indi_scopelink
.RE
.PP
Then connect a client and set
.B DEVICE_PORT
to the controller's port. Prefer the per-unit name under
.I /dev/serial/by-id/
to
.IR /dev/ttyACM n,
which is renumbered whenever another CDC device is plugged in first.
.SH SIMULATION
Enabling the standard INDI
.B SIMULATION
switch before connecting makes the driver answer itself, with no port opened.
.B SIMULATED_GENERATION
on the Options tab selects which hardware generation it imitates, which is what makes the differences
between them visible. See
.BR scopelink-simulator (1)
for the same simulated controller served on a pseudo terminal instead.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/share/indi/indi_scopelink.xml
Driver list entry, which is how clients find the driver.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/udev/rules.d/99-scopelink.rules
Access rights for the controller.
.TP
.I ~/.indi/ScopeLink_config.xml
Saved device configuration.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR scopelink-cli (1),
.BR scopelink-simulator (1),
.BR indiserver (1)
.PP
Full documentation, including the Ekos walkthrough, is at
.UR https://drivers.indilib.org/focusers/astrolabs/scopelink/scopelink
.UE .
